{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And when the sun sets and he is clean, then he may eat.</b> The entering of his sunset holds him back from eating terumah, but washing his body does not hold him back from eating terumah." "<b>Then he may eat of the holy things.</b> The verse speaks of terumah. And if you ask: if there is a warning concerning terumah, why is it stated concerning holy things, and if it is stated concerning holy things, why is it stated concerning terumah? Rather, because there is in terumah something unique, for it was not permitted to a non-priest, unlike holy things, upon which one is liable on account of פגול, נותר, and טמא — which is not so with terumah — therefore it is necessary to state a warning concerning holy things, and it is necessary to state a warning concerning terumah."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:14.522237282Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}